After twenty weeks of work, the new desk opened on Monday. Read the details on the [project page](/projects/service-desk-consolidation/).

The opening was quiet, which the team had planned for. Agents took their first calls with a senior colleague on the line, and the knowledge base was open on every screen. By the end of the first week, most questions were answered without a transfer.

Residents now have one number to call. The desk answers in the language they speak, and a short message explains what will happen next. If a request needs a specialist, the agent stays on the line until it reaches the right person.

We would like to thank the staff of the three former teams. They gave us honest feedback in every workshop, and many of their suggestions are now part of the daily routine.

The city will review the figures in the spring. We will publish a short summary when they are ready.
